{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Strange Stories"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "What Happened to Her?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Relate information about problems."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le05ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect vs. Past Simple "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect </span>:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "</li><li>For something that started in the past and continues in the present. </li></ul> Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> I have learned a lot in this class.</span> <br><br> </li><li>For something that has been done several times. </li></ul>Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">She has called her mom many times. </span> <br> <br></li><li>For experiences up to the present. </li></ul> Example: <br><span class=\"italic\">This is the worst day we've ever had.</span> <br><br></li><li> For something that happened in the past but is relevant at the time of speaking. </li></ul>  Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> I can't call her. I've lost my cellphone. </span> <br> <br> </li><li>For referring to a time that is not yet finished. </li></ul> Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Have you played guitar this week?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\"> Simple Past for</span>: <br></li><li>  Something that was finished at a certain period of time. </li></ul>  Example: <br>  <span class=\"italic\">I wrote that letter two weeks ago. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you can answer the question 'When?', the past time is stated or inferred or understood. Use the Past Simple. There is no connection to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the you cannot answer the question 'When?', because the time is not stated or not important, then choose the Present Perfect tense. There is instead a connection to the present."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sentence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">When she finished, she paid her bill and mine.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" when she finished (her coffee)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> She's just come in again with the director ... </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  from the time she left  to now\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "A strange young woman came into the coffee shop. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She looks like she's been through a war!  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I didn't mean to be nosy, but she looked like she's had a really bad day. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Did she need help? "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect Continuous vs Present Perfect"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense </span> to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about experience. When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense </span>, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. <br> To emphasize the result of the action, use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect </span>.<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Has anyone called the police?</span></li></ul> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Continuous tense </span> to describe:<ul><li> a single activity that lasts a long time, and</li><li> an action that is repeated over a long period of time.</li></ul>These continue up to the present. You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Continuous tense</span> when a long activity has just stopped. <br> To emphasize the action, use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Continuous</span>.<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">What have the other people in the cafe been doing?</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sentence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She's just been staring into space.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She is spending a long time doing this - focus is on <span class=\\\"italic\\\">staring </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Has she been mugged? Is she in shock? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What happened before this sometime?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Everyone here has been ignoring her - like it's normal. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She's covered in mud. How could that have happened?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It hasn't been raining."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to stare into space"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to look at nowhere"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She's just been staring into space."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to describe an odd event in a cafe."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be mugged"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be robbed of your personal belongings"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Has she been mugged?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be in shock"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be deeply surprised and troubled by a sudden event "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Is she is shock?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mud"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "wet, soft earth"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She's covered in mud."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to ignore"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to actively not notice or recognize"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Everyone here has been ignoring her - like it's normal."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "nosy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "overly curious"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I said I didn't mean to be nosy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to recognize someone"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to realize that someone is famous"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I recognized her immediately and felt so stupid!!!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob06aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "autograph"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person's signature"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did you get her autograph?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob06aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Outline a storyline that you can text a friend or classmate about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make sure you have all the details ready."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Let the friend or classmate know that you will be texting them in English about something that happen and what has happened."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Let them know you expect them to ask questions or make comments English."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you are finished texting, look over the texts together and comment of spelling and grammar mistakes."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I make up a storyline for an event I can text about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I text a friend or classmate to tell them using the Past Simple tense and the Present Perfect tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I go over the texts with my friend or classmate looking for mistakes."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss coincidences, strange events or superstitions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about things that happened or have happened."},